        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft, mildly tender suprapubically and in the right inguinal region; no guarding or rebound, no mass, bowel sounds normal. No obvious inguinal hernia on attempted Valsalva."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-20",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-20",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal and testicular examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left testis descended, normal size and consistency, non-tender, no mass. Right hemiscrotum enlarged and tense, not erythematous or hot, with mild diffuse tenderness especially superiorly; transilluminates, consistent with hydrocele. Right testis itself difficult to palpate clearly; no discrete hard mass felt. No scrotal skin breakdown despite pad use. No obvious inguinal hernia with cough/strain, although examination limited by cooperation."
      }
    },
    {
